Day 1 Project Report – Project Setup & UI Development
Project Setup & User Interface

On Day 1, the primary focus was on setting up the project structure and developing the basic user interface for the Login and Registration modules.
The objective was to create a clean, responsive, and user-friendly interface that can be extended with backend functionality in the upcoming stages.
First, the project environment was configured and the required folders and files were organized properly.
A structured project architecture was created to separate components, pages, assets, and other resources.
This structure will help maintain the project efficiently and make future development easier.
The Login page was developed with input fields for essential user credentials such as email/username and password.
Proper labels, buttons, spacing, and basic validation considerations were included to provide a simple and clear user experience.
A Registration page was also created to allow new users to enter their required information and create an account.
The interface was designed consistently with the Login page so that users can easily navigate between the two pages.
The project also includes separate interface considerations for User and Admin login.
The purpose of this design is to provide different access levels based on the type of user.
The Admin interface can later be connected with administrative features, while the User interface can be connected with regular user functionalities.
